        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The two equal middle entries in row $2n-1$ of Pascal’s triangle add to give the single middle entry in row $2n$.",
          "worked": "Row $2n-1$ of Pascal’s triangle has two equal middle entries. The addition rule gives the single middle entry of row $2n$ by adding these two entries, so it is double either one. These entries are the coefficients specified in part (a).",
